// The pool — the programs a guest may be tonight.
//
// A CHARACTER with nothing but a name (no hooks, no beats, not `listed`)
// has no part in the story, so the app offers it on the guest sign-in
// picker instead of the performer one. Each is one guest's for the night:
// once claimed it is greyed out for everyone else. A guest who wants to be
// something not on this list searches the program directory (Wikipedia,
// software only — never antivirus) and picks one of that article's pictures.
// The nine featured programs (cast/featured.loom) are on the same picker.
//
// Profile pictures are hand-picked: `avatar: File:…` names a Wikipedia /
// Commons file (the server downloads it when the story loads), and
// `a | b` offers more than one — the first is the default, and a guest
// chooses between them plus the article's own gallery at sign-in.
// `wiki:` names the article when the program's name alone would find the
// wrong one (Minesweeper the ship). Every pool program carries an
// `avatar:` so no picture needs a lookup on the night.
//
// Trojan Horse is the two accordion clowns' costume: one program, one
// phone (a shared identity is new code, see README).

